      "content": "thanks. i guess i'm just struggling with how to make it feel real. i keep thinking that there's this line between just writing about the darkness and actually becoming part of it. like, can art even be truly honest if it's just words on a page? or is the only way to reach that level of \"surrender\" you mentioned to actually let go of everything for real? i'm trying to figure out if the ultimate expression of that theme would be the act itself rather than just the poem about it.",
